1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,099
When an agent forgets, the whole team starts over.

2
00:00:03,099 --> 00:00:07,003
Engram Collective gives agents a shared memory, a visible chain

3
00:00:07,003 --> 00:00:09,792
of evidence, and a way to carry work forward.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,958
A coordinator plans the work.

5
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:16,996
Researchers and builders can run in parallel.

6
00:00:16,996 --> 00:00:19,966
Verifiers test the actual artifacts, while a

7
00:00:19,966 --> 00:00:23,409
curator turns completed work into useful knowledge.

8
00:00:23,409 --> 00:00:26,784
Handoffs carry evidence, files and remaining work.

9
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,447
Episodes preserve what happened.

10
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:33,937
Semantic memory keeps sourced facts and corrections.

11
00:00:33,937 --> 00:00:37,561
Procedural memory stores tools and verified workflows.

12
00:00:37,561 --> 00:00:41,386
Engram combines pinned context, a recent memory cache and

13
00:00:41,386 --> 00:00:45,345
graph retrieval, while Mem zero extracts and refines facts.

14
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:49,786
A corrected fact is more than a new sentence.

15
00:00:49,786 --> 00:00:52,705
Engram follows the tasks that depended on the

16
00:00:52,705 --> 00:00:55,689
old fact, marks their results stale, and links

17
00:00:55,689 --> 00:00:57,959
a revised plan to the new evidence.

18
00:00:57,959 --> 00:01:01,203
The causal timeline makes that change inspectable.

19
00:01:02,867 --> 00:01:05,664
When agents disagree, both claims survive.

20
00:01:05,664 --> 00:01:08,528
Each keeps its source and observation time.

21
00:01:08,528 --> 00:01:11,059
The resolver selects the latest active

22
00:01:11,059 --> 00:01:13,323
evidence under an explicit policy.

23
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:16,587
Contradictory claims at the same timestamp remain

24
00:01:16,587 --> 00:01:19,784
unresolved, instead of becoming false certainty.

25
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,915
A reusable procedure is bound to exact

26
00:01:23,915 --> 00:01:27,975
artifact versions, preconditions and passing source checks.

27
00:01:27,975 --> 00:01:32,517
A different verifier must execute its own tests before activation.

28
00:01:32,517 --> 00:01:35,063
Reuse runs check those same files and

29
00:01:35,063 --> 00:01:38,367
record actual model usage and execution savings.

30
00:01:39,867 --> 00:01:42,311
Every tenant has a separate graph.

31
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:44,325
Memory can belong to a team,

32
00:01:44,325 --> 00:01:45,691
a user or an agent.

33
00:01:45,691 --> 00:01:48,998
Code runs in isolated Docker sandboxes with no

34
00:01:48,998 --> 00:01:52,306
network, a read only root and resource limits.

35
00:01:52,306 --> 00:01:57,339
Safeguard judges memory admission; it does not grant tool permissions.

36
00:01:58,867 --> 00:02:02,918
Postgres preserves conversations, task state and checkpoints.

37
00:02:02,918 --> 00:02:06,438
FalkorDB keeps relationships and causal dependencies.

38
00:02:06,438 --> 00:02:10,556
Qdrant supports Mem zero, with local embeddings for retrieval.

39
00:02:10,556 --> 00:02:14,342
Across separate live and infrastructure fixtures, restart

40
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:18,195
checks preserved sessions, artifact files and checkpoints.

41
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,038
This is Engram Collective: an agent team designed

42
00:02:23,038 --> 00:02:25,899
to remember, coordinate and show its work.

43
00:02:25,899 --> 00:02:30,939
This walkthrough combines real app captures and infrastructure validation.

44
00:02:30,939 --> 00:02:33,255
The complete Qwen team run remains

45
